    "text": "atlantanewsfirst.com\nwebsite\nGwinnett County, Georgia\n2 arrested on drug trafficking charges in Gwinnett County, GBI says\nBy Atlanta News First staff,8 hours ago\nATLANTA, Ga. (Atlanta News First) - Two suspects are facing possible deportation after officers arrested them on drug trafficking charges in Gwinnett County. On Wednesday, July 2, officers with the Appalachian Regional Drug Enforcement Office (ARDEO) — a multi-agency unit that covers 30 counties in north Georgia — arrested 35-year-old Hector Moreno Luzardo and 41-year-old Gelis Escalona Martinez, both of Venezuela, on charges of trafficking in methamphetamine and trafficking in cocaine, according to the Georgia Bureau of Investigation (GBI).\n4\nComments / 1\nLoading editor...",
